2026-09-04  Robert Charusta  <rch-public@posteo.net>

	Replace global regular expressions with action-aware fontification.

	* go-template-mode-font-lock.el: New file.
	(go-template-mode-font-lock--double-quoted-special-regexp)
	(go-template-mode-font-lock--single-quoted-special-regexp): Use literal
	character classes available in Emacs 28.1.
	(go-template-mode-font-lock--clear-action-properties): Use text property
	search primitives available in Emacs 28.1.
	(go-template-mode-font-lock-install): New current-buffer integration API.
	(go-template-mode-font-lock-uninstall): Likewise.
	(go-template-mode-font-lock--scan-quoted)
	(go-template-mode-font-lock--scan-ordinary): Skip ordinary input runs
	with search primitives instead of scanning every character in Lisp.
	Implement complete action, comment, string, trim-marker, variable,
	field, action-word, constant, and predefined-function scanning with
	standard Font Lock-managed faces and multiline invalidation.
	* go-template-mode.el (go-template-mode): Use the shared fontification
	library.  Disable buffer-wide syntactic strings and remove HTML tag
	highlighting.  Bump version to 2.0.0.
	* tests/go-template-mode-test.el: Replace minimal offset-based tests
	with action-scope, HTML-attribute, vocabulary, malformed-input,
	lifecycle, and incremental-refontification coverage.
	* tests/font-lock-manual.gotmpl: New file.  Add a committed manual
	visual regression fixture.
	* Makefile (SOURCES): Compile both production Lisp files.
	* README.org: Document action-scoped behavior, host-mode composition,
	the shared API, manual visual checks, development commands, and current
	limitations.
	* PROVENANCE.md: New file.  Record historical sources and the 2.0.0
	rewrite boundary.
	* NEWS: New file.  Record user-visible release changes.
	* ChangeLog: Rename from CHANGELOG for GNU file-name conventions.

